  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New `xtask/src/budget.rs`: one job budget for each gate run. The default is 6 (`budget::DEFAULT`). `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=<n>` (1 or more) overrides it. A bad value prints a note and keeps 6.\n- `exec.rs` sets `-j` and `--test-threads=` of each step when it runs the step (`budget::scale`):\n  - A wave of N lanes gives each lane `budget / N` jobs, minimum 1.\n  - A step that runs alone gets the full budget. This applies to each quick, batch and test step, and to each release step that runs alone.\n  - A value that a step sets on purpose (not the plan default `6`) can only go down.\n- `lanes::waves(steps, limit)` takes the lane limit. The release tier gives `budget::lane_limit` = `budget / 2`, minimum 1. `LIMIT = 4` is removed. A budget of 6 gives 3 lanes of 2 jobs.\n- The gate prints the budget line at the start, and `-- wave K: N lane(s) x -j M` before each wave. `--dry-run` prints the same lines.\n- The `gate` and `runners` skills have the rule: the sum of `-j` of all builds on one machine stays at or below its core count.\n- `docs/decisions/2057-gate-job-budget.md` records the choices.\n\n## Overlap with #1952 (#1941)\n\nThe plan builders (`plan.rs`, `quick.rs`, `single.rs`) do not change. The executor rewrites the flags at run time. Thus each step that #1952 adds also gets the budget. `git merge-tree` of this branch with the head of #1952 is clean, so this PR does not stack on it. After the two PRs merge, one line of `docs/decisions/1941-gate-step-per-binary.md` (\"four at most\") is old. The cut can correct it when it collects the decisions.\n\n## Readings\n\n`cargo xtask gate release --dry-run` (start):\n\n```\ngate budget: 6 job(s) (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS overrides); at most 3 lane(s) per wave; 1 lane(s) x -j 6, 2 lane(s) x -j 3, 3 lane(s) x -j 2\n-- wave 1: 1 lane(s) x -j 6\n[01] debug build (--no-run)\n...\n-- wave 3: 3 lane(s) x -j 2\n[03] geometry suites\n     (cwd issue-2057) cargo test -j 2 -p camcraft-geometry --no-fail-fast -- --test-threads=2\n```\n\n`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run` prints `gate budget: 4 job(s); steps run one at a time with -j 4` and `-j 4 ... --test-threads=4` on each step.\n\n## Pinning tests (`xtask/src/budget_tests.rs`)\n\n- `wave_jobs_sum_to_at_most_the_budget_and_lanes_to_at_most_half` (budgets 1 to 16)\n- `budget_six_gives_three_lanes_of_two_jobs`\n- `a_step_alone_keeps_the_full_budget`\n- `scale_keeps_deliberate_values_low_and_child_args_alone`\n- `the_override_must_be_a_whole_number_of_one_or_more`\n\nThe `lanes_tests.rs` tests now give the limit 4 explicitly. The executor test sets the budget to 6, so that its two lanes overlap with each value of `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS`.\n\nGate: `cargo test -j 2 -p xtask -- --test-threads=2` (143 + 3 + 3 passed), `cargo clippy -j 2 -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean), `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real batch or release gate ran. A post-merge gate was in progress and the machine had a high load.\n- The wall times of one batch run and one release wave, before and after, were not measured. The \"Done means\" item for them is still open; the next release gate or post-merge run gives the \"after\" value.\n- The budget does not see other builds on the machine (reviews, workers). The skills give that rule to each build.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2057\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
